WEBVTT

00:02.480 --> 00:03.647
Water...

00:04.857 --> 00:06.358
Earth...

00:06.818 --> 00:08.402
Fire...

00:08.945 --> 00:10.320
Air.

00:11.281 --> 00:14.616
Long ago, the four nations
lived together in harmony.

00:15.451 --> 00:19.413
Then, everything changed
when the Fire Nation attacked.

00:19.747 --> 00:22.666
Only the Avatar,
master of all four elements,

00:22.750 --> 00:23.959
could stop them.

00:24.043 --> 00:25.585
But when the world needed him most,

00:25.670 --> 00:26.920
he vanished.

00:27.422 --> 00:28.672
100 years passed,

00:28.756 --> 00:31.008
and my brother and I
discovered the new Avatar--

00:31.092 --> 00:32.634
An airbender named Aang.

00:33.011 --> 00:35.012
And although
his airbending skills are great,

00:35.096 --> 00:37.723
he has a lot to learn
before he's ready to save anyone.

00:37.807 --> 00:38.807
Oof!

00:39.183 --> 00:42.102
But I believe Aang can save the world.

01:04.792 --> 01:06.043
Would you sit down?!

01:06.127 --> 01:08.170
If we hit a bump,
you'll go flying off!

01:08.254 --> 01:09.504
What's bugging you anyway?

01:10.048 --> 01:11.590
It's what Avatar Roku said.

01:11.674 --> 01:13.508
I'm supposed to master
all four elements

01:13.593 --> 01:14.885
before that comet arrives.

01:14.969 --> 01:15.969
Well, let's see.

01:16.054 --> 01:17.554
You pretty much mastered airbending,

01:17.638 --> 01:19.431
and that only took you 112 years.

01:19.807 --> 01:20.807
I'm sure you can master

01:20.892 --> 01:22.184
three more elements by next summer.

01:22.935 --> 01:24.561
I haven't even started waterbending,

01:24.645 --> 01:26.730
and we're still weeks away
from the North Pole.

01:26.981 --> 01:28.482
What am I gonna do?!

01:28.566 --> 01:29.566
Calm down.

01:29.650 --> 01:30.776
It's gonna be ok.

01:31.486 --> 01:32.486
If you want,

01:32.570 --> 01:33.570
I can try and teach you

01:33.654 --> 01:34.654
some of the stuff I know.

01:34.739 --> 01:35.739
You'd do that?

01:36.407 --> 01:37.407
We'll need to find

01:37.492 --> 01:38.658
a good source of water first.

01:39.702 --> 01:41.620
Maybe we can find a puddle
for you to splash in.

01:44.707 --> 01:45.707
Nice puddle.

01:56.260 --> 01:57.386
Yeah!

01:57.470 --> 01:58.720
Don't start without me, boy!

01:58.805 --> 02:00.389
Remember the reason we're here.

02:00.473 --> 02:01.473
Right.

02:01.557 --> 02:02.849
Time to practice waterbending.

02:03.601 --> 02:05.560
Great. So, what am I supposed to do?

02:05.853 --> 02:07.396
You could clean the gunk

02:07.480 --> 02:08.480
out of Appa's toes.

02:10.149 --> 02:12.192
So, while you guys
are playing in the water,

02:12.276 --> 02:13.527
I'm supposed to be hard at work

02:13.611 --> 02:15.612
picking mud
out of a giant bison's feet?

02:15.863 --> 02:16.863
Mud and bugs.

02:19.200 --> 02:20.200
Ok.

02:29.168 --> 02:30.419
Whoa! Whoa!

02:30.503 --> 02:31.711
Oof!

02:31.796 --> 02:32.879
Someone's changing our course.

02:35.925 --> 02:37.175
What's the meaning of this mutiny?

02:37.260 --> 02:38.885
No one told you to change course.

02:39.345 --> 02:41.012
Actually, someone did.

02:41.431 --> 02:42.431
I assure you,

02:42.515 --> 02:44.891
it is a matter of utmost importance,

02:44.976 --> 02:46.059
Prince Zuko.

02:46.602 --> 02:47.894
Is it something to do with the Avatar?

02:48.438 --> 02:49.855
Even more urgent.

02:49.939 --> 02:51.148
It seems I--

02:51.232 --> 02:52.941
I've lost my lotus tile.

02:54.485 --> 02:55.610
Lotus tile?

02:55.903 --> 02:57.737
For my pai sho game.

02:57.822 --> 02:59.614
Most people think the lotus tile

02:59.699 --> 03:00.824
insignificant.

03:01.367 --> 03:04.703
But it is essential
for the unusual strategy

03:04.787 --> 03:06.538
that I employ.

03:06.622 --> 03:09.624
You've changed our course
for a stupid lotus tile?

03:09.709 --> 03:11.585
See, you, like most people,

03:11.669 --> 03:13.670
underestimate its value.

03:13.921 --> 03:16.089
Just give me 10 minutes
to check the merchants

03:16.174 --> 03:17.507
at this port of call.

03:17.592 --> 03:20.760
Hopefully, they'll have
the lotus tile in stock

03:20.845 --> 03:23.305
and I can get on with my life.

03:26.184 --> 03:29.227
I'm lucky to have such
an understanding nephew.

03:32.940 --> 03:34.065
Yeah, don't get too happy.

03:34.150 --> 03:35.192
You've got to do me next.

03:37.528 --> 03:38.862
This is a pretty basic move,

03:38.946 --> 03:41.031
but it still took me
months to perfect.

03:41.491 --> 03:42.782
So, don't be frustrated

03:42.867 --> 03:44.159
if you don't get it right away.

03:45.161 --> 03:47.829
Just push and pull the water
like this.

03:47.914 --> 03:49.873
The key is getting
the wrist movement right.

03:51.417 --> 03:52.417
Like this?

03:55.254 --> 03:56.588
That's almost right.

03:57.048 --> 03:58.131
If you keep practicing,

03:58.216 --> 03:59.341
I'm sure eventually--

03:59.425 --> 04:00.842
Hey, I'm bending it already!

04:01.219 --> 04:03.553
Wow! I can't believe
you got that so quickly.

04:04.180 --> 04:06.264
It took me two months
to learn that move.

04:06.349 --> 04:07.516
Well, you had to figure it out

04:07.600 --> 04:08.767
all on your own.

04:08.851 --> 04:10.477
I'm lucky enough
to have a great teacher.

04:10.978 --> 04:11.978
Thanks.

04:12.438 --> 04:13.647
So, what's next?

04:13.731 --> 04:15.357
This is a more difficult move.

04:15.441 --> 04:17.317
I call it streaming the water.

04:20.696 --> 04:21.863
It's harder than it looks,

04:21.948 --> 04:23.073
so don't be disappointed if...

04:34.043 --> 04:35.085
Nice work.

04:35.169 --> 04:37.420
Though the over-the-head
flair was unnecessary.

04:38.047 --> 04:39.047
Sorry.

04:39.131 --> 04:40.507
Well, don't stop now.

04:40.591 --> 04:41.758
Keep 'em coming.

04:41.842 --> 04:43.510
Well, I kind of know
this one other move,

04:43.970 --> 04:45.220
But it's pretty hard.

04:45.304 --> 04:46.972
I haven't even totally
figured it out yet.

04:47.431 --> 04:50.684
The idea is to create
a big, powerful wave.

04:56.274 --> 04:57.440
So, like this?

05:02.780 --> 05:03.780
Aang!

05:12.081 --> 05:13.665
Looks like I got
the hang of that move.

05:13.749 --> 05:15.000
What else you got?

05:15.084 --> 05:16.710
That's enough practicing for today.

05:17.086 --> 05:18.420
Yeah, I'll say!

05:18.504 --> 05:20.005
You just practiced our supplies

05:20.089 --> 05:21.089
Down the river.

05:21.173 --> 05:22.924
Sorry.

05:23.259 --> 05:24.759
I'm sure we can find some way

05:24.844 --> 05:25.844
to replace all this stuff.

05:26.095 --> 05:27.220
My life was hard enough

05:27.305 --> 05:28.388
when you were just an airbender.

05:39.275 --> 05:40.900
Please, put me down!

05:40.985 --> 05:42.944
See the wonder in this bag!

05:43.487 --> 05:46.114
Who's brave enough
to look into this bag?!

05:46.198 --> 05:47.198
Wow!

05:50.202 --> 05:52.245
We've got exactly
three copper pieces left

05:52.330 --> 05:53.663
from the money that King Bumi gave us.

05:53.748 --> 05:55.123
Let's spend it wisely.

05:55.374 --> 05:57.667
Make that
two copper pieces, Sokka.

05:58.085 --> 05:59.461
I couldn't say no to this whistle.

06:03.424 --> 06:04.591
It doesn't even work.

06:07.637 --> 06:10.055
See? Even Momo thinks
it's a piece of junk.

06:10.514 --> 06:11.765
No offense, Aang,

06:11.849 --> 06:13.516
but I'll hold the money from now on.

06:18.939 --> 06:21.149
Earth Nation! Fire Nation!

06:21.233 --> 06:22.484
Water Nation.

06:22.568 --> 06:25.153
So long as bargains
are your inclination,

06:25.237 --> 06:26.780
you're welcome here!

06:26.864 --> 06:27.947
Don't be shy.

06:28.032 --> 06:29.741
Come on by!

06:30.076 --> 06:31.493
You there!

06:31.577 --> 06:33.536
I can see from your clothing

06:33.621 --> 06:35.497
that you're world traveling types.

06:35.581 --> 06:37.082
Perhaps I can interest you

06:37.166 --> 06:39.209
in some exotic curios?

06:39.502 --> 06:40.585
Sure!

06:40.670 --> 06:41.836
What are curios?

06:44.215 --> 06:46.007
I'm not entirely sure,

06:46.092 --> 06:47.217
But we got 'em.

07:03.192 --> 07:07.362
I've never seen
such a fine specimen of lemur.

07:07.738 --> 07:09.781
That beast would fetch me a hefty sum

07:09.865 --> 07:11.866
if you'd be interested in bartering.

07:15.621 --> 07:16.621
Momo's not for sale.

07:26.173 --> 07:27.465
Look at this, Aang!

07:27.550 --> 07:29.509
It's a waterbending scroll.

07:29.927 --> 07:31.636
Check out these crazy moves.

07:32.138 --> 07:34.556
Where did you get
a waterbending scroll?

07:35.182 --> 07:37.642
Let's just say I got it up north

07:37.727 --> 07:39.477
at a most reasonable price--

07:39.854 --> 07:40.854
Free.

07:43.858 --> 07:45.442
Wait a minute.

07:45.526 --> 07:46.985
Sea-loving traders

07:47.069 --> 07:49.446
with suspiciously acquired merchandise

07:50.114 --> 07:52.240
and pet reptile birds?

07:52.658 --> 07:54.159
You guys are pirates!

07:54.660 --> 07:56.494
We prefer to think of ourselves as

07:56.579 --> 07:57.996
high-risk traders.

07:59.623 --> 08:02.292
So, how much for the traded scroll?

08:02.668 --> 08:03.918
I've already got a buyer--

08:04.003 --> 08:05.920
A nobleman in the Earth Kingdom--

08:06.338 --> 08:08.673
Unless, of course, you kids have

08:08.758 --> 08:11.634
200 gold pieces on you right now.

08:11.719 --> 08:13.511
I know how to deal
with these guys, Katara.

08:13.888 --> 08:14.888
Pirates love to haggle.

08:17.433 --> 08:19.267
Watch and learn.

08:19.977 --> 08:22.479
What say ye to the price of...

08:22.563 --> 08:24.022
One copper piece?

08:24.940 --> 08:26.649
Ha ha ha ha!

08:26.734 --> 08:29.277
The price is 200 gold pieces.

08:29.653 --> 08:31.946
I don't haggle on items this rare.

08:32.198 --> 08:34.741
Ok, two copper pieces.

08:35.284 --> 08:37.619
It's not as amusing
the second time, boy.

08:37.870 --> 08:39.662
Aang, can we get out of here?

08:39.747 --> 08:41.414
I feel like we're getting weird looks.

08:41.874 --> 08:44.292
Aye! We be casting off now!

08:45.002 --> 08:46.711
What was that all about, Katara?

08:46.796 --> 08:48.630
Yeah, I was just starting
to browse through

08:48.714 --> 08:49.798
their boomerang collection.

08:50.299 --> 08:51.466
I'll just feel a lot better

08:51.550 --> 08:52.592
once we get away from here.

08:53.135 --> 08:54.219
Hey, you!

08:54.303 --> 08:55.553
Get back here!

08:55.638 --> 08:56.679
Well, well.

08:56.764 --> 08:58.306
Look who's come to their senses.

08:58.808 --> 09:00.141
Told you the haggling would pay off.

09:12.029 --> 09:13.196
There they are!

09:13.280 --> 09:14.280
Get 'em!

09:14.365 --> 09:16.324
Nobody's going nowhere!

09:19.370 --> 09:21.037
I don't think these pirates

09:21.121 --> 09:22.330
are here to trade with us.

09:22.414 --> 09:23.957
Get back here!

09:24.041 --> 09:25.667
You little--

09:25.751 --> 09:26.793
Come on!

09:27.127 --> 09:28.127
This way.

09:28.212 --> 09:29.295
Let's cut 'em off!

09:31.423 --> 09:36.135
Whoa!

09:36.220 --> 09:37.220
Oof!

09:51.110 --> 09:52.485
My cabbages!

09:52.570 --> 09:54.195
This place is worse than Omashu!

10:01.328 --> 10:02.328
Aha!

10:05.624 --> 10:06.833
I hope that lemur of yours

10:06.917 --> 10:08.167
has nine lives.

10:10.880 --> 10:13.298
Now, who gets to taste

10:13.382 --> 10:15.425
the steel of my blade first?

10:15.509 --> 10:16.759
No, thanks.

10:17.511 --> 10:18.511
Haa!

10:20.848 --> 10:22.140
Grab on tight!

10:22.224 --> 10:23.600
Aang, I thought we were

10:23.684 --> 10:25.143
running away from the pirates.

10:25.561 --> 10:26.811
Just hang on.

10:26.896 --> 10:27.979
Whoa!

10:29.773 --> 10:31.232
Whoa!

10:34.695 --> 10:36.487
I used to kind of look up to pirates,

10:36.572 --> 10:37.989
but those guys are terrible.

10:38.073 --> 10:39.157
I know.

10:39.241 --> 10:41.200
That's why I took this.

10:41.619 --> 10:42.619
No way!

10:42.703 --> 10:44.037
Isn't it great?!

10:44.121 --> 10:45.830
No wonder they were
trying to hack us up.

10:46.165 --> 10:48.124
You stole their waterbending scroll.

10:48.208 --> 10:49.876
I prefer to think of it as

10:49.960 --> 10:51.586
high-risk trading.

10:51.670 --> 10:52.670
Ha ha ha.

10:52.755 --> 10:54.213
Good one, Katara.

10:54.298 --> 10:56.299
Sokka, where to you think they got it?

10:56.592 --> 10:58.593
They stole it from a waterbender.

10:59.053 --> 11:00.136
It doesn't matter.

11:00.220 --> 11:01.679
You put all of our lives in danger

11:01.764 --> 11:02.764
just so you could learn

11:02.848 --> 11:04.515
some stupid, fancy splashes.

11:04.934 --> 11:07.602
These are real waterbending forms.

11:07.686 --> 11:08.895
You know how crucial it is

11:08.979 --> 11:10.563
for Aang to learn waterbending.

11:12.191 --> 11:13.399
Whatever.

11:13.484 --> 11:14.776
Well, what's done is done.

11:14.860 --> 11:15.944
We have it.

11:16.028 --> 11:17.236
We might as well learn from it.

11:26.163 --> 11:28.748
I've checked all the shops
on this pier.

11:28.832 --> 11:32.377
Not a lotus tile
in the entire marketplace.

11:32.920 --> 11:33.920
It's good to know this trip

11:34.004 --> 11:35.004
was a complete waste of time

11:35.089 --> 11:36.381
for everyone!

11:36.465 --> 11:37.840
Quite the contrary.

11:38.467 --> 11:40.802
I always say
the only thing better than

11:40.886 --> 11:43.096
finding something you are looking for

11:43.681 --> 11:46.557
is finding something
you weren't looking for

11:46.642 --> 11:48.935
at a great bargain.

11:49.979 --> 11:51.646
You bought a sungi horn?

11:51.730 --> 11:53.231
For music night on the ship.

11:53.691 --> 11:55.817
Now, if we only had some woodwinds.

11:57.820 --> 11:59.862
This place looks promising.

12:01.240 --> 12:03.574
That is handsome!

12:03.951 --> 12:06.327
Wouldn't it look
magnificent in the galley?

12:06.412 --> 12:07.912
We lost the water tribe girl

12:07.997 --> 12:08.997
and the little bald monk

12:09.081 --> 12:10.581
she was traveling with.

12:10.666 --> 12:12.625
This monk, did he have
an arrow on his head?

12:15.254 --> 12:16.921
I just want to try
this one move first,

12:17.006 --> 12:18.214
and then it's all yours.

12:18.298 --> 12:19.298
Here, hold it open for me.

12:23.178 --> 12:24.554
The single water whip.

12:25.014 --> 12:26.431
Looks doable.

12:32.604 --> 12:33.604
Ha ha ha!

12:33.689 --> 12:35.023
What's so funny?

12:35.107 --> 12:36.816
I'm sorry, but you deserved that.

12:36.900 --> 12:38.109
You've been duped.

12:38.193 --> 12:39.861
She's only interested
in teaching herself.

12:39.945 --> 12:41.279
Aang will get his turn

12:41.363 --> 12:42.697
once I figure out the water whip.

12:47.745 --> 12:49.912
Why can't I get
this stupid move?!

12:49.997 --> 12:50.997
You'll get it.

12:53.667 --> 12:55.126
You've just gotta shift your weight

12:55.210 --> 12:56.461
through the stances.

12:57.004 --> 12:58.129
There. See?

12:58.213 --> 12:59.213
The key to bending is--

12:59.298 --> 13:01.174
Will you please shut your air hole!

13:01.258 --> 13:02.884
Believe it or not,
your infinite wisdom

13:02.968 --> 13:04.552
gets a little old sometimes!

13:05.012 --> 13:06.637
Why don't we just
throw the scroll away

13:06.722 --> 13:09.265
since you're so naturally gifted?!

13:10.893 --> 13:11.893
What?!

13:14.772 --> 13:16.481
My gosh, Aang.

13:16.565 --> 13:18.274
I am so sorry.

13:18.734 --> 13:20.276
I don't know what came over me.

13:20.778 --> 13:21.903
But you know what?

13:21.987 --> 13:23.362
It won't happen again.

13:23.739 --> 13:25.031
Here, this is yours.

13:25.282 --> 13:26.282
I don't want to have

13:26.366 --> 13:27.784
anything to do with it anymore.

13:28.243 --> 13:29.285
It's ok, Katara.

13:29.578 --> 13:30.620
What about Momo?

13:30.704 --> 13:32.080
He's the real victim here.

13:32.164 --> 13:33.289
I'm sorry, Momo.

13:33.540 --> 13:34.749
And what about me?

13:34.833 --> 13:35.833
There was that time you--

13:35.918 --> 13:37.043
No more apologies.

13:48.847 --> 13:50.681
Shouldn't we stop to search the woods?

13:50.891 --> 13:52.058
We don't need to stop.

13:52.142 --> 13:53.768
They stole
a waterbending scroll, right?

13:55.354 --> 13:56.729
Then they'll be on the water.

14:17.501 --> 14:18.543
Shh.

14:18.627 --> 14:20.837
Momo, go back to sleep.

14:23.757 --> 14:24.757
Shh!

14:35.853 --> 14:36.894
Shoot!

14:36.979 --> 14:39.272
Come on, water! Work with me here!

14:39.898 --> 14:41.524
Ok, what if I-- Ow!

14:44.111 --> 14:45.153
Ok, Katara,

14:45.237 --> 14:47.155
shift your weight through the stances.

14:54.621 --> 14:56.539
No!

14:56.623 --> 14:57.623
Let go of me!

15:00.210 --> 15:01.878
I'll save you from the pirates.

15:10.554 --> 15:11.846
Tell me where he is,

15:11.930 --> 15:13.264
and I won't hurt you or your brother.

15:13.348 --> 15:14.348
Go jump in the river!

15:16.310 --> 15:17.727
Try to understand,

15:17.811 --> 15:18.936
I need to capture him

15:19.021 --> 15:20.188
to restore something I've lost--

15:20.606 --> 15:21.731
My honor.

15:22.399 --> 15:23.566
Perhaps in exchange,

15:23.650 --> 15:24.859
I can restore something you've lost.

15:27.362 --> 15:28.946
My mother's necklace.

15:29.865 --> 15:30.948
How did you get that?!

15:31.283 --> 15:32.283
I didn't steal it

15:32.367 --> 15:33.451
if that's what you're wondering.

15:33.911 --> 15:35.661
Tell me where he is.

15:35.746 --> 15:36.746
No!

15:36.830 --> 15:38.664
Enough of this necklace garbage.

15:39.041 --> 15:41.125
You promised the scroll.

15:41.835 --> 15:43.753
I wonder how much money this is worth.

15:43.837 --> 15:45.129
No!

15:45.714 --> 15:46.881
A lot, apparently.

15:47.507 --> 15:49.592
Now, you help me find what I want,

15:49.676 --> 15:50.801
you'll get this back,

15:50.886 --> 15:52.637
and everyone goes home happy.

15:53.180 --> 15:55.264
Search the woods for the boy
and meet back here.

15:55.349 --> 15:56.349
Fine.

16:02.564 --> 16:03.689
Where did she go?

16:04.066 --> 16:05.149
I don't believe it.

16:06.318 --> 16:07.318
What's wrong?

16:07.402 --> 16:08.444
She took the scroll.

16:08.528 --> 16:09.779
She's obsessed with that thing.

16:09.863 --> 16:11.155
It's just a matter of time

16:11.240 --> 16:12.323
before she gets us all in deep--

16:12.407 --> 16:13.658
Whoa!

16:26.463 --> 16:27.755
I've got him. Come on!

16:28.215 --> 16:30.925
What?
I'm not good enough to kidnap?

16:31.260 --> 16:32.343
Aagh!

16:36.098 --> 16:37.223
Nice work.

16:43.605 --> 16:45.106
Aang, this is all my fault.

16:45.649 --> 16:46.816
No, Katara, it isn't.

16:47.025 --> 16:48.442
Yeah, it kind of is.

16:49.861 --> 16:51.112
Give me the boy.

16:51.280 --> 16:53.447
You give us the scroll.

16:53.949 --> 16:55.783
You're really gonna
hand over the Avatar

16:55.867 --> 16:57.827
for a stupid piece of parchment?

16:57.911 --> 16:59.078
Don't listen to him.

16:59.162 --> 17:00.705
He's trying to turn
us against each other.

17:01.331 --> 17:03.291
Your friend is the Avatar?

17:03.375 --> 17:04.417
Sure is.

17:04.501 --> 17:06.210
And I'll bet he'll fetch a lot more

17:06.295 --> 17:08.129
on the black market
than that fancy scroll.

17:08.630 --> 17:09.797
Shut your mouth,

17:09.881 --> 17:11.048
you water tribe peasant!

17:11.466 --> 17:14.260
Yeah, Sokka,
you really should shut your mouth.

17:14.720 --> 17:15.970
I'm just saying,

17:16.054 --> 17:17.388
it's bad business sense.

17:17.472 --> 17:18.764
Just imagine how much the Fire Lord

17:18.849 --> 17:20.308
would pay for the Avatar.

17:20.559 --> 17:22.518
You guys would be set for life.

17:22.936 --> 17:24.437
Keep the scroll.

17:24.521 --> 17:26.230
We can buy 100 with the reward

17:26.315 --> 17:27.523
we'll get for the kid.

17:28.025 --> 17:30.401
You'll regret breaking a deal with me.

17:52.632 --> 17:53.674
Thanks, Momo.

17:53.759 --> 17:55.343
I owe you a bushel of apples.

18:22.120 --> 18:23.120
Hey!

18:35.675 --> 18:36.675
Aah!

18:37.094 --> 18:39.136
Aang, are you there?

18:39.221 --> 18:41.347
I'm over here! Follow my voice.

18:41.681 --> 18:43.432
Where? I can't find you!

18:43.517 --> 18:44.642
I'm right here!

18:49.398 --> 18:50.689
Never mind.

18:50.941 --> 18:51.982
I'll find you!

18:53.276 --> 18:54.777
Run!

18:56.613 --> 18:58.155
Katara, you're ok.

18:58.532 --> 18:59.949
Help me get this boat
back in the water

19:00.033 --> 19:01.158
so we can get out of here.

19:05.539 --> 19:06.831
We need a team of rhinos

19:06.915 --> 19:08.040
to budge this ship.

19:08.125 --> 19:09.375
A team of rhinos...

19:09.459 --> 19:11.293
Or two waterbenders.

19:22.139 --> 19:23.305
Everybody in!

19:26.643 --> 19:28.144
Are you so busy fighting

19:28.228 --> 19:29.812
you cannot see your own ship

19:29.896 --> 19:31.522
has set sail?

19:31.606 --> 19:33.441
We have no time
for your proverbs, uncle.

19:33.942 --> 19:35.192
It's no proverb.

19:36.903 --> 19:38.362
Bleeding hog monkeys!

19:39.114 --> 19:40.531
Ha ha ha ha!

19:45.078 --> 19:47.371
Hey, that's my boat!

19:47.456 --> 19:49.498
Maybe it should be a proverb.

19:49.583 --> 19:50.583
Come on, uncle.

19:54.171 --> 19:56.338
Sokka, can't you make it
go any faster?

19:56.631 --> 19:58.007
I don't know how.

19:58.091 --> 19:59.717
This thing wasn't made
by the water tribe.

20:07.058 --> 20:11.312
Whoa!

20:15.984 --> 20:17.026
Oof!

20:17.527 --> 20:19.153
Hey! You did the water whip.

20:19.488 --> 20:21.030
I couldn't have done it
without your help.

20:21.364 --> 20:23.032
Will you two quit
congratulating each other

20:23.116 --> 20:24.158
and help me out?

20:41.051 --> 20:42.301
That's good.

20:43.011 --> 20:44.220
Wah!

20:44.304 --> 20:45.387
Hah!

20:51.770 --> 20:53.062
Aang, look!

20:56.024 --> 20:57.483
No!

21:05.116 --> 21:06.951
Aah!!

21:07.035 --> 21:08.494
Have you lost your mind?

21:08.578 --> 21:10.704
This is no time for flute practice!

21:12.666 --> 21:13.832
We can stop the boat.

21:13.917 --> 21:15.167
Aang, together,

21:15.252 --> 21:16.377
push and pull the water.

21:24.052 --> 21:25.135
It's working.

21:25.220 --> 21:26.220
It's slowing down.

21:33.728 --> 21:34.853
We're doing it!

21:34.938 --> 21:36.272
But we have another problem.

21:38.733 --> 21:40.025
Whoa! Whoa!

21:41.945 --> 21:43.153
Jump!

21:58.712 --> 22:01.130
I knew a bison whistle
would come in handy.

22:01.464 --> 22:02.548
Thanks, Appa.

22:02.632 --> 22:04.008
Yeah, we owe you one.

22:07.679 --> 22:08.721
My boat!

22:14.728 --> 22:15.811
Prince Zuko,

22:15.895 --> 22:17.896
you're really going to
get a kick out of this.

22:18.773 --> 22:22.651
That lotus tile
was in my sleeve the whole time!

22:31.620 --> 22:32.703
Aang,

22:32.787 --> 22:34.330
I still owe you an apology.

22:35.165 --> 22:36.749
You were just so good at waterbending

22:36.833 --> 22:38.208
without really trying.

22:38.293 --> 22:39.710
I got so competitive

22:39.794 --> 22:41.086
that I put us all in danger.

22:41.713 --> 22:42.838
I'm sorry.

22:43.298 --> 22:44.757
That's ok, Katara.

22:44.841 --> 22:47.801
Besides, who needs
that stupid scroll anyway?

22:47.886 --> 22:50.095
Is that really how you feel?

22:50.180 --> 22:51.305
The scroll!

22:51.389 --> 22:53.140
First, what did you learn?

22:53.558 --> 22:54.767
Stealing is wrong.

22:56.645 --> 22:57.978
Unless it's from pirates.

22:58.355 --> 22:59.438
Ha ha ha!

22:59.522 --> 23:00.648
Good one, Katara.
